      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The expansion of state surveillance for national security is inherently a violation of the social contract because it fundamentally breaks the trust required for a free society to function. The social contract demands that the state protects individual liberty in exchange for obedience, but mass surveillance turns citizens into subjects rather than free partners, effectively ending the very freedom the government claims to uphold. Any argument that this is a \"necessary evolution\" is a dangerous lie that justifies tyranny under the guise of safety.",
